ue in the election  is that is that junk history or is that  I don't I I don't know I've never seen  any convincing evidence of that it could  be true in hindsight it was completely  unnecessary the Paris peace talks  weren't making any progress at all  Hubert Humphrey campaign whenever he was  asked what he was going to do about the  war in Vietnam he merrily said you know  Humphrey have this weirdly merry way of  talking and he would say say oh I I  don't have to worry about that that'll  be all over by the time I'm in the White  House  but in fact there was no progress being  made so I I don't know I mean I've heard  those stories I've never seen any  evidence of that in trying to explain  why the events of 1968 occurred in 1968  could you mention maybe the coming of  age of the baby boomers as having an  influence there yeah  sure it did not least of all because it  meant that there were an enormous number  of people going to college and colleges  especially in Europe were becoming very  overcrowded which was leading to a lot  of student dissatisfaction this in fact  was a major issue in most European  universities was the overcrowding yeah  sure so what happened  I remember 68 there were different  values I remember money was bad the army  was bad drugs were good  no but seriously if people were trying  we're looking differently for a  different value system non consumerist  value system and there were a lot of  people think it seemed like everybody  was on the left then what what happened  well first of all everybody wasn't on  the left that's part of the problem you  know one of the great lessons from 68  which came as such a surprise to all of  us but shouldn't have been is that if  you decide to try to change the world  the people who are controlling the world  are going to be pretty ruthless about  stopping you and in the United States  Richard Nixon completely reconfigured  politics and reconstructed a different  Republican Party I mean the Republican  Pa